WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.930
Shine a lamp on a piece of pondweed,

2
00:00:01.980 --> 00:00:05.510
and it gives off a
stream of tiny bubbles.

3
00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:08.550
Move the lamp closer,
and you get more bubbles.

4
00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:11.190
Closer again, more still.

5
00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:14.230
Then you reach a point where
moving it closer makes no more

6
00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:15.450
difference.

7
00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:18.090
Why does extra light stop helping?

8
00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:21.150
In this mission, you'll see how
counting the bubbles measures

9
00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:22.770
the rate of photosynthesis.

10
00:00:22.820 --> 00:00:25.730
You'll find out how light intensity,

11
00:00:25.780 --> 00:00:28.870
carbon dioxide and temperature
each affect that rate.

12
00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:31.930
And you'll meet the idea
of a limiting factor,

13
00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:34.570
and what it does to a graph.

14
00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:38.490
Your mission: explain why
more light stops helping.
